# =============================================================================
# TEMPLATE — adapted from LogicLoom's own .github/workflows/plugin-tests.yml.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES
#   Runs your project's own test suite on every push and every pull request.
#   LogicLoom's own copy of this file runs ~40 named bash contract-test scripts
#   under tests/contract/ — that list is OUR harness's own suite and does not
#   ship to an adopter (the adopt payload excludes tests/ and
#   .logic-loom/tests/ outright, since they test the harness, not your
#   project). This template does NOT reproduce that list. It gives you the
#   same SHAPE — checkout, set up your runtimes, run your tests, fail the
#   build red on any failure — with your own test command in the one step
#   that matters.
#
# WHAT IT ASSUMES
#   - GitHub-hosted runners (`ubuntu-latest`). Self-hosted runners work too;
#     nothing here depends on GitHub-hosted specifically.
#   - You have ONE command that runs your whole suite (`npm test`, `pytest`,
#     `go test ./...`, `bash tests/run_all_tests.sh`, ...). If you have
#     several independent suites, duplicate the "Run tests" step per suite —
#     the way LogicLoom's own copy has one named step per contract script —
#     rather than chaining them with `&&`, so a CI failure names which suite
#     broke instead of just "the tests step failed."
#
# WHAT TO CHANGE (placeholders below, marked ⟨LIKE THIS⟩)
#   - ⟨RUNTIME SETUP⟩ — delete the setup-node / setup-python steps you don't
#     need, or add the ones your project actually requires (Ruby, Go, JVM...).
#   - ⟨YOUR TEST COMMAND⟩ — replace with the real command. If you don't have
#     one yet, that's the actual gap this file is meant to surface — write one
#     before wiring the workflow, not after.
#   - The job name and the `Run tests` step name are generic on purpose;
#     rename them to whatever your team calls the suite.
#
# WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT INCLUDE
#   LogicLoom's own copy also runs two REPO-SPECIFIC fail-closed gates —
#   check-generated-freshness.sh (a generated artifact matches its sources)
#   and check-brain-record.sh (the `.brain/` knowledge-layer record holds
#   together). Both are LogicLoom mechanisms your project may not have adopted
#   (`.brain/` ships README-only until you opt in — see
#   `/initialize-project`'s `.brain/` scaffold step). If you use them, add
#   your own steps calling those scripts; this template does not assume you
#   do.
# =============================================================================

name: Tests

on:
  push:
  pull_request:

jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      # ⟨RUNTIME SETUP⟩ — keep what you need, delete the rest.
      - name: Set up Node.js
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '20'   # ⟨YOUR NODE VERSION⟩

      - name: Set up Python
        uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: '3.11'   # ⟨YOUR PYTHON VERSION, IF NEEDED⟩

      - name: Run tests
        run: echo "⟨YOUR TEST COMMAND HERE — e.g. npm test, or bash tests/run_all_tests.sh⟩" && exit 1
